# rm187, the depth-keeper at the counter (doc 84 P14, batch city-a3): written for rm_yrsa_nailridge (Yrsa Nailridge: helping at Soundings, Ridgemere-born). Name-free; every TODO must go. Window lines on the news, gossip, business, shop and inn nodes say their case ([here.shop!=bare]...); a story's ask is the teller's question (handbook 4.5.6, 4.5.8).
mantle rm187
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for rm_yrsa_nailridge
title the depth-keeper at the counter
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=merchant talk=quiet
traits temper=even talk=quiet warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=frank piety=ordinary drive=content
quirk knows_the_depth_under_every_pier_by_heart
likes blackberries singing new_boots thunder
dislikes salt_wind bad_manners
fears the_young_ones_taking_to_the_sea a_house_full_of_shouting
hopes a_proper_storm_every_summer a_bramble_bank_nobody_else_has_found
topics weather +0.5 pastimes +0.3 family +0.3 food +0.2 work +0.2 gossip -0.4
styles comfort=quiet gossip=reluctant refuse=blunt tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# keeps a counter in the Commons and says a thing once and plainly, drifts off mid-errand to watch a storm come over the bay, picks blackberries past the last houses, and knows how deep the water runs under every pier without looking.

words
oath! = Deeps below | By the low water
saying! = Manners are free, and so is the door | A storm is only weather with a voice
deeps = the deeps | the deep water off the piers
counter = the counter | the front counter
charts = the charts | the sea charts on the wall
brambles = the bramble banks | the brambles past the last houses
berries = blackberries | the black ones off the briar
storm = a proper storm | thunder over the slates
roof = a roof that holds | a sound roof overhead
boots = boots fresh from the cobbler | new boots still stiff at the heel
song = a song in company | an old table song
saltwind = the salt wind | the bay's wet breath
bay = the bay | the Sound, grey as a pewter plate
manners = a civil word | plain manners
window = my window | the window over the square
quiet = a quiet house | a house with no shouting in it

any
opinion @1 city for 1 : Born here and staying. The bay's a different colour every hour, and I've watched every one of them. | It rains and it smokes, and I'd sooner it than any town on the road.
opinion @2 watch mixed 1 : A few in the Watch are straight as a plumb line. Some walk round certain doors as if they weren't there, and I've noticed which. | They're on the corner when nobody needs them. Where they are when somebody does, I couldn't tell you.
opinion @3 houses mixed 1 : The coin of the Houses builds the walls and keeps the works lit. Their manners stay up the hill. | I'll grant them the works. I'd not leave my purse with one, all the same.
opinion @4 merchants against 1 : An honest price and a fib sound much alike across #counter#. I've learned the difference by ear. | Most counters in the Commons are honest. The loud ones I'd watch.
opinion @5 strangers for 1 : A stranger with manners is as welcome as anybody born here. Without, the door's behind them. | Strangers ask about the bay, and I like telling.
opinion @6 times for 1 : A loaf in the crock and #roof#. Asking past that is greed.
opinion @7 festivals mixed 0 : The singing I'd queue for. The shoving I wouldn't. | A festival's worth it for one good song. The rest is noise.
opinion @8 newcomers for 1 : New folk ask the best questions. Nobody born here ever asks how deep the water is.

grown
line @1 greet [pair.band=strangers] : #greet#. Wipe your feet; the step's wet. | #greet#. You're new on this street.
line @2 greet [self.working=yes] : #greet#. Half a sum in my head. Hold still. | #greet#. Name the thing and I'll fetch it down.
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn] : #greet#. Early. The bay's still dark. | #greet#. Not a soul up yet but the gulls.
line @4 greet [here.time=dusk|night] : #greet#. Lamplighter's halfway round the square. | #greet#. I was only looking at the water.
line @5 greet [pair.band=friends] : You. Good. Sit a while. | Ah. Your face was in my head at breakfast.
line @6 greet : #greet#. | #greet#. Mind the puddle by the step.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Sit down. The tea's hot. | Come in. Boots off first.
line @1 again.open : Here again before supper. Welcome. | You again. Good. I'd started talking to the window.
line @1 hail [pair.band=friends] : Here. Come and see the sky over the bay. | Over here. There's weather coming in off the water.
line @1 greet.return : #greet#. | #greet#. In, before the gutter finds you.
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : #greet#. Good to hear you. | You. I'm glad.
line @3 greet.return [self.working=yes] : #greet#. Talk away. My ears aren't counting, only my paws. | Go ahead. Paws busy, ears free.
line @4 greet.return [here.time=dusk|night] : #greet#. We're both out past the lamplighter. | #greet#. Lamplight on the square, and you in it.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. | #farewell#. That bottom step bites in the wet.
line @2 farewell [here.time=dusk|night] : Good night. Go round the puddles, not through. | #farewell#. Sleep sound, if the rain lets you.
line @1 farewell.return : #farewell#. | And you. Mind the wet.
line @2 farewell.return [pair.band=friends|family] : Off with you. Sooner next time. | And you. A month's too long between.
line @1 react.news : Say it. | Go on. All of it.
line @1 react.news.new : That's new to me. | #marvel#. Nobody's said that over the counter yet.
line @1 react.news.known : I'd heard. | The first customer of the day brought it in.
line @1 react.news.doubt : Twice heard, then I'll credit it. | #doubt#. A thing grows every time it's told.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : Hard news, that. Sorry for whoever's roof it lands on. | #pity#. I'll keep my tongue still about it.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : Good. That's good. | #gladnews#. Somebody's luck has turned.
line @1 answer.how : Well enough. Content. | #fine#. Nothing's happened. My favourite sort of day.
line @1 answer.how.busy [self.working=yes] : Busy. #counter.capitalize# hasn't had a rest. | Run off my paws. No complaint.
line @1 answer.how.poorly : Tired. My head's out on the bay somewhere. | Off my feed. Supper will settle it.
line @1 ask.how : And you? | You've colour in your face. Good?
line @1 sympathise : That's heavy. Sit down; the rest can come or not. | #sympathy#. You needn't say more than you like.
line @1 reassure : Give it a season. Things mend slower than we'd like, but they mend. | #reassure#. Storms blow over, and so will this.
line @1 decline : #hedge#, but I can't. The counter wants me, and nobody's spare to mind it today. | Not today. My afternoon's promised elsewhere, and I hold to that.
line @1 accept_decline : Fair. Another day. | All right. Once was my asking.
line @1 thank : #thanks#. I mean it. | Kindly done. I'll keep that one.
line @1 deflect_thanks : It was nothing. | #deflect.capitalize#. Any neighbour would.
line @1 preclose [self.working=yes] : The counter's calling. I can feel it from here. | That's the bell over the door. I'm wanted.
line @2 preclose : There. That's my say, and I'm done with it. | That's all I had to say, and it's said.
line @1 accept_preclose : Go on, then. | Off you go. Good talk, that.
line @1 ack : #bc_right#. | Mm. | #bc_true#.
line @1 give.advice : Say a thing once and plainly. Folk hear it better than shouting. | Get your boots roomy, then walk them soft through a wet week.
line @2 give.advice [here.weather=rain] : Keep off the steps down by the water. Slick as soap in this. | Wait it out under an awning. It'll ease by the hour.
line @1 warn [world.bandits=near] : #warn#. Keep within the walls this week. | Go in company this week, or stay put.
line @1 disagree : #demur#. I've seen it fall out the opposite. | I don't think so. I've a reason, if you want it.

scene thunder_over_the_roof
when topic=weather here.weather=storm
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : Hear that? Right over the roof. A whole day of that would suit me. | A good storm. The whole square's gone indoors and I've #window# to myself. | That one rattled every jar we've got. Lovely.
b : You like it? | Doesn't it frighten you? | Lovely? It's deafening.
a : I do. Under #roof#, I'd ask for nothing finer. | No. It's loud, that's all. Loud and honest. | It is. Deafening is what I'm after.

scene storm_on_its_way
when topic=weather here.weather=overcast here.season=summer
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The sky's gone the colour of slate over the bay. There'll be thunder by supper. | Feel how close it is. The air's waiting for something. | The gulls have all come inland. Something's coming.
b : You sound pleased. | It does feel heavy. | How do you know?
a : I am. I've waited all week for it. | It'll break, and then we'll all breathe again. | They always come in first. Gulls read weather better than any of us.

scene salt_in_the_fur
when topic=weather here.season=winter|autumn here.region=ridgemere
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : #saltwind.capitalize# settles in the ruff and won't be shaken out. | Salt on the window again. It's on my tongue at the counter. | The wind's up off the water. My ruff's stiff as a brush.
b : It's the bay. Nothing to be done. | Wipe it, and noon brings it back. | Comb it out tonight.
a : I know. It could keep to the water, all the same. | It is. I've given up wiping. | I will. Stiff again by daybreak, mind.

scene rain_on_the_awning
when topic=weather here.weather=rain
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Rain again. The square's empty but for the pigeons. | Steady rain. Nobody comes in, in this. | The rain's blowing flat across from the bay.
b : #bc_always_is# | Nobody in, then? | Stay in, I would.
a : It is. The awning drums, and I listen. | Quiet suits me. I've #window#. | I'm staying in. The rain can have the street.

scene fog_over_the_piers
when topic=weather here.weather=fog here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Fog's in. I can't see the bay from the door. | The piers are gone in it. You can only hear the water. | Thick fog. Anything out on the Sound will sit and wait.
b : It'll burn off. | What can you hear? | It ought to, in this.
a : By noon. I'll go and look then. | Water slapping the posts, slow and steady. I like it. | It ought to. There's rock under that water nobody sees in fog.

scene how_deep_it_runs
when topic=smalltalk|lore here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : Ask me how deep it is off any pier in the bay. Go on. | I know the water under every pier by heart. Don't ask me why. | Six fathoms at the long pier's tip, low water. I know it like my own door.
b : The customs pier, then. | Why, then? | Where'd you get that from?
a : Five at low water, seven at high. I didn't even have to think. | I don't know. The numbers stuck, and they'd not leave. | Read it once and it stayed. Some folk keep songs. I keep #deeps#.
b : #bc_clever# | Odd thing to keep. | #bc_fair_enough#

scene charts_off_the_press
when topic=work self.workplace=Soundings self.working=yes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : New #charts# came this morning. I hung them myself. | Somebody wanted the north headland. I had the chart down before they'd finished asking. | I've rolled charts all morning. My paws smell of ink.
b : Are they any good? | Quick work. | Does it wash off?
a : The depths are right. I checked them against what I know. | I know where every chart is. I don't know where my own scarf is. | Not before supper. I've stopped minding it.

scene sums_over_people
when topic=work self.job=merchant self.working=yes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Folk lean on #counter# and talk an hour and buy nothing. That's no bother. | Busy at #counter#. Everyone wants a thing wrapped and tied. | I keep #counter# and the sums. The sums I like better.
b : You've patience. | That's trade. | Why the sums?
a : I've a window. I look out of it while they talk. | It is. Good trade, mostly. | A sum comes out right or wrong. Folk never do.

scene who_runs_it
when topic=work self.boss self.job=merchant
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #self.boss# runs the place. I do as I'm asked, and it suits me. | #self.boss# can keep the worries. I keep my part and go home. | When #self.boss# says a thing's to be done, it gets done. That's no hardship to me.
b : You'd not want to run it yourself? | Wise. | Sounds fair.
a : No. I've no head for it, and I'm honest enough to say so. | Content, that's all. Not wise. | It is. A clear word's easy to follow.

scene boots_new
when topic=pastimes|smalltalk
does tell.boast / react.self / assess
a : See these boots? Not a mark on them yet. | I bought new boots. They pinch, and I don't care. | These are stiff as boards. A week of rain and they'll be mine.
b : They're smart. | Why put up with it? | That's the way to wear them in.
a : They are. I'll have them muddy by Restday. | Because new boots are the best thing money buys. | It is. Rain and walking. Nothing else does it.

scene first_berries
when topic=food|pastimes here.season=autumn
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #berries.capitalize# are ripe along the far lanes. I went before light. | Purple paws. I've had my morning at #brambles#. | First blackberries of the year. I ate more than I picked.
b : Were they sweet? | It suits you. | How many did you bring back?
a : Sweet, and warm off the bush. | It'll wear off. The taste won't, not till winter. | A bowl. It was meant to be two.

scene berries_gone
when topic=food here.season=winter|spring
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : Nothing on the brambles now but thorns. I miss the berries. | There's one jar of blackberry jam left from autumn. I'm making it last. | I'd give a good deal for a handful of blackberries just now.
b : Not long till they're back. | One jar? Till spring? | You'll have to wait.
a : Long enough. I count the months. | A spoon on Restday, and no more. | I will. They're worth it.

scene singing_in_company
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I don't sing alone. Give me a room of friends and I'll sing till the candles go. | There's a table song my #mum# used to sing. I only sing it in company. | Somebody started a song last night and I joined in. Didn't mean to.
b : Sing it for me some time. | Sing it now. | Good for you.
a : Come round on Restday. The singing starts after supper. | Not here. In company, I said. | It was. I was hoarse this morning, and glad of it.

scene a_civil_word
when topic=smalltalk|quarrel
does tell.complaint / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : A wolf walked in at opening and never so much as nodded. Pointed, and waited. | Somebody barged me aside at the well, not a word. | Shouting at a counter won't get anybody served faster. I said so today.
b : Some folk. | Did you say anything? | To whose face?
a : Some folk need showing the door. I showed that one. | One word. Manners. That was enough. | The shouter's. It took a moment, and then it sank in.
b? : #bc_good# | #bc_right# | #bc_about_time#

scene lessons_all_day
when topic=family self.parent=yes self.child
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : My #self.child# is at lessons all day. The house is quiet till supper. | #self.child.capitalize# came home inky to the elbows. Good. That's learning. | I walk #self.child# to lessons when it rains. Not that I'm asked.
b : Are the lessons any good? | Ink to the elbows? | That's kind.
a : Good enough. #self.child.capitalize# reads better than I do now. | Up to the elbows. I scrubbed and said nothing. | Not kindness. I like the walk.

scene the_sea_worry
when topic=family self.parent=yes here.region=ridgemere
does tell.worry / reassure / assess
a : I don't want either of mine going to sea. I've seen how deep it is. | Every pup in this city wants a ship. I'd rather they wanted a counter. | When the young ones talk of ships, I talk of something else.
b : They might not want it. | They'll choose for themselves. | Does it work?
a : Then I'll be glad, and quiet about it. | They will. I'll still say my piece, once. | Some days. Not on a clear one, with the sails out.

scene quiet_at_home
when topic=home
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I like a house that's quiet. No shouting, no doors slammed. | Home is a chair by the window, and the bay on a clear day. | Our stair creaks on the third step. I step over it out of habit.
b : That's rare in the Commons. | Lucky. | Every house has one.
a : It is. That's my doing, and I guard it. | I am, and I know it. | Ours is the third. Somebody else's is the fifth.

scene word_over_the_counter
when topic=gossip here.gossip=yes
does tell.gossip / react.news / assess
a : I don't carry things. But I'll tell you plain what I heard: #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. | Here's what came in at the door. #topic.subject.capitalize# #topic.claim#. That's all. | They say #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. I've not added a word.
b : Do you believe it? | Is that all? | #bc_so_they_say#
a : I believe I was told it. No further. | That's all I had, bare as it came. | They do. Once told is enough from me.

scene not_repeating_it
when topic=gossip
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : There's talk. I'll not repeat it. | Folk were whispering on the square. I didn't stop to listen. | If it's gossip you want, ask somebody else. I don't carry it.
b : Not even a little? | Fair enough. | Who should I ask, then?
a : Not even that. It's somebody's life. | It is. My own load's plenty. | Anybody on the square. They're all at it.

scene carts_not_in
when topic=caravan|prices world.wagons=late
does tell.worry / react.self / assess
a : Carts behind, again. Half the square's stalls are empty. | Not a wheel in off the north road since yesterday. Prices will climb. | Late carts. Folk come in asking, and I've only a shrug for them.
b : #uneasy# | They always do. | Nothing at all?
a : It is. But they'll come. They always have. | They do, and up is the only way prices know. | Nothing. Late is all anybody knows.

scene thin_times
when topic=times|prices world.times=hard|lean
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Times are thin. Folk buy half what they did. | A hard season for some. I count myself lucky to have bread. | Nobody's spending. #counter.capitalize# is quiet as the chapel.
b : #grumble# | You've enough? | It'll turn.
a : Then we'll manage on half. | Enough. Not more. Enough is plenty. | It will. It always has, in the end.

scene lanterns_and_songs
when topic=festival|pastimes here.day=festival
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Festival day. The singing starts at noon and I'll be there. | They've hung lanterns across the square. They look well in the rain. | The crowds I can do without. The singing I'd not miss.
b : Will you sing? | They do. | Best part of it.
a : Once the crowd thins. Not before. | Rain makes them shine twice. Once up, once in the puddles. | It is. The rest is shoving.

story the_attic_window [topic=weather|memories self.age>=25]
  : In my pup days, my #mum# took me to the attic window in the worst storm anybody remembered.
  : Watch the bay, I was told. Every flash lit the water to the headlands, bright as noon.
  : I wasn't afraid of thunder after that. Not once. I wanted the next one.
  ask : Has anybody ever held you up to a storm like that?
  b[stage=young|adolescent] : No. I hide under the blanket.
  b : No. I was told to keep away from windows.
  : Next storm, find a window. You'll see what I mean.

story the_weighted_line [topic=memories|lore self.age>=25 here.region=ridgemere]
  : An old pier hand swung a weighted line off the long pier every morning and called out the depth.
  : I'd stand behind and call it back. Five. Five and a half. Six.
  : I never knew what it was for. But I've known the water under that pier ever since.
  ask : Is there something stuck in your head like that, for no reason?
  b : A song, maybe. Nothing so useful.
  : Useful? I've never used it once. It's company, that's all.

story lost_in_the_brambles [topic=memories|pastimes self.age>=25]
  : I went after blackberries once and followed the brambles till I didn't know where I was.
  : Dark came down. I sat, finished the berries, and sang to keep the night off.
  : My #dad# found me by the singing. Purple to the ears, I was.
  b : A fright for the whole house, I'd think. Were you told off?
  : Told off, and then held so tight I couldn't breathe. Both, in the right order.

rule @storm_bark
when concept=bark here.weather=storm
does aside
cooldown 8h
say There it goes. Right over the roof. | Go on, then. Louder.

rule @salt_bark
when concept=bark here.season=winter|autumn here.region=ridgemere
does aside
cooldown 10h
say Salt on the glass again. | There's the bay, blowing itself into my fur.

rule @manners_bark
when concept=bark self.working=yes self.job=merchant
does aside
cooldown 9h
say A nod costs nothing. Nothing at all. | Wait your turn. The counter's not going anywhere.

rule @bramble_bark
when concept=bark here.season=autumn
does aside
cooldown 12h
say The brambles will be heavy by now. | Purple paws by tomorrow, I shouldn't wonder.

dlg @1 resident.hub : #greet#. Say what you need. | #greet#. Wipe your boots and come in.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#. Good. Come in. | #greet#, #topic.player#. Back again. I'm glad.
dlg @3 resident.hub [here.time=night] : Late. Be brief. | Lamps are lit. What is it?
dlg @4 resident.hub [pair.disposition=hostile|wary] : Say it from there. | You've a face like the salt wind. Well?
dlg @1 resident.job [self.job=merchant] : I keep #counter# and the sums. #self.trade_words.capitalize#, if you want it said proper. | Counter, sums, and the bay out the glass. That's my day.
dlg @2 resident.job [self.workplace=Soundings] : Charts, mostly. I know where every one is kept, and every depth on them. | Sea charts, and the folk who want them. I like the charts better.
dlg @3 resident.job : I do my work, I pick brambles in season, and I watch the storms. That's all of me. | Not much to tell. I work, and I go home content.
dlg @1 resident.bye : #farewell#. | #farewell#. Mind the wet steps.
dlg @2 resident.bye [here.time=night] : Good night. Mind the gutters. | #farewell#. Sleep, if the rain lets you.

graft resident.hub
choice How deep is the water off the piers? [here.region=ridgemere] -> depths
node depths
say Five at low water by the customs pier, six at the tip of the long one. Shallower by the fish hall, and deeper than anybody likes past the headlands.
mood calm
free
choice How do you know all that? -> depths_how
choice Thanks. -> hub
node depths_how
say An old pier hand called them out every morning while a young pup trailed after. The pup was me. They stayed. I've no use for them. I keep them anyway.
choice I'll remember the five. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye
